-- Slice 6 (nested-module soundness), the LEGIT-POLYMORPHISM accept -- the
-- positive counterpart to `reject/t51`-`t54`: a nested unannotated
-- `fn id(x) do x end` used at BOTH `Int` and `String` in the same nested
-- module. This is exactly the code the P0 prebind fix must keep accepting.
-- Notably it was ALSO broken pre-fix, but in the OTHER direction: the stale
-- qualified-prebind placeholder pinned `id` to its FIRST use, so a second use
-- at a different type spuriously ERRORED (`id` was accidentally monomorphic,
-- not polymorphic). The fix reconciles the qualified key to `id`'s real
-- body-checked scheme `a -> a`, RESTORING legitimate let-polymorphism while
-- closing the launder. A second, independent witness that the fix neither
-- over-restricts nor over-monomorphises. See core-march-types.md §2.8.13.
mod Outer do
  mod App do
    fn id(x) do x end

    fn both() : Int do
      let a = id(42)
      let b = id("hi")
      a + string_length(b)
    end
  end
end
